Fix AOT IL2087 and IL2090 warnings in these files in `/tmp/sv-d38ddb5ecad2454b9682fbd3bab61741/before/`.

## 1. ArmOperation.cs - Lines 98 and 104

The method `IsResource<T>()` uses `typeof(T).GetConstructor(...)` (line 98) and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)` (line 104). Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the type parameter `T`.

Current code (lines 96-111):
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<T>() where T : notnull
{
    var isResource = typeof(T).GetConstructor(
                    BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance,
                    null,
                    CallingConventions.Any,
                    new Type[] { typeof(ArmClient), typeof(ResourceIdentifier) },
                    null) is not null;
    var obj = Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance, null, null, null);
    if (!isResource && obj is not IJsonModel<object>)
    {
        throw new InvalidOperationException($"Type {typeof(T)} should be Resource or Model");
    }

    return isResource;
}
```

Fix: Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` to `T`:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```

Make sure `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` is present in the using statements. If not, add it.

## 2. GenericOperationSource.cs - Lines 37 and 40

The class `GenericOperationSource<T>` uses `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)` on line 40 and `ModelReaderWriter.Read(response.Content, typeof(T))` on line 37. Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the class's type parameter `T`.

Current code:
```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<T> : IOperationSource<T>
```

Fix: Change to:
```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>
```

The `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` is already present in this file.

## 3. ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs - Line 30

The method `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` calls `builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration)` which has `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]`.

Current code (lines 27-31):
```csharp
public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(this TBuilder builder, TConfiguration configuration)
    where TBuilder : IAzureClientFactoryBuilderWithConfiguration<TConfiguration>
{
    return builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration);
}
```

Fix: Add `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]` attributes to the method:
```csharp
[RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator (EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator=true) instead.")]
[RequiresDynamicCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values requires generating dynamic code at runtime, for example instantiating generic types. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator (EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator=true) instead.")]
public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(this TBuilder builder, TConfiguration configuration)
    where TBuilder : IAzureClientFactoryBuilderWithConfiguration<TConfiguration>
{
    return builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration);
}
```

Make sure `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` is present in the using statements. It's already imported at line 4.

## 4. ArmEnvironment.cs - Line 80

`JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)` in `ToString()`. Replace with manual JSON construction.

Current: `public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);`

Fix - write the JSON manually:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    using var stream = new System.IO.MemoryStream();
    using (var writer = new Utf8JsonWriter(stream))
    {
        writer.WriteStartObject();
        writer.WriteString("Endpoint", Endpoint.ToString());
        writer.WriteString("Audience", Audience);
        writer.WriteString("DefaultScope", DefaultScope);
        writer.WriteEndObject();
    }
    return System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(stream.ToArray());
}
```

Make sure `using System.Text.Json;` is present (it already is).

## 5. ArmClientOptions.cs - Line 52

`JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span)` in `SetApiVersionsFromProfile`.

Replace with `JsonDocument.Parse` approach. 

Current code around line 52:
```csharp
var span = BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span;
var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);
var armProfile = allProfile["resource-manager"];
```

Fix: Replace with JsonDocument-based parsing:
```csharp
var span = BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span;
using var profileDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(span);
var armProfile = profileDoc.RootElement.GetProperty("resource-manager");
```

Then update the iteration below to work with JsonElement instead of Dictionary. Read the file first to see the full loop and adapt it.

## 6. LRO files - `.ToObjectFromJson<Dictionary<string, string>>()`

Four files have the same pattern at line 61:
- `ManagementGroup/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ManagementGroupsArmOperation.cs`
- `ManagementGroup/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ManagementGroupsArmOperationOfT.cs`
- `Resources/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ResourcesArmOperation.cs`
- `Resources/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ResourcesArmOperationOfT.cs`

Current (all have same line):
```csharp
var lroDetails = ModelReaderWriter.Write(rehydrationToken, ModelReaderWriterOptions.Json, AzureResourceManagerContext.Default).ToObjectFromJson<Dictionary<string, string>>();
return lroDetails["id"];
```

`.ToObjectFromJson<T>()` calls `JsonSerializer.Deserialize<T>()` internally. Replace with `JsonDocument.Parse` approach:
```csharp
var binaryData = ModelReaderWriter.Write(rehydrationToken, ModelReaderWriterOptions.Json, AzureResourceManagerContext.Default);
using var lroDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(binaryData);
return lroDoc.RootElement.GetProperty("id").GetString();
```

This eliminates the need for `Dictionary<string, string>` deserialization entirely.

